{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"institution":[{"name":"Optica Open"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2023,1,31]],"date-time":"2023-01-31T06:13:51Z","timestamp":1675145631837},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2023,1,31]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Optica Publishing Group","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2023,1,31]],"date-time":"2023-01-31T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1675123200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc-sa\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":[],"abstract":"<jats:p>In this work, the general temporal phase unwrapping (TPU) algorithm is described as a weighted sum of wrapped phases, followed by a rewrapping process to remove integer multiples of 2\u03c0. Then, we propose dual-sensitivity phase unwrapping using the scalar relation between a synthetic non-wrapped estimation and one of the high-modulation phases. This two-stage approach allows TPU algorithms to preserve the original signal-to-noise ratio (SNR). An optimized method considering the relative phase modulations is also proposed, allowing us to successfully use TPU in conditions where fixed-coefficients algorithms would fail. Mathematical derivation, numerical simulations and experimental results are presented.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1364\/opticaopen.21964997","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,1,31]],"date-time":"2023-01-31T00:12:32Z","timestamp":1675123952000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Optimized algorithms for temporal phase unwrapping without degrading the signal-to-noise ratio"],"prefix":"10.1364","author":[{"given":"Moises","family":"Padilla","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Manuel","family":"Servin","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Gonzalo","family":"Paez","